WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:05.624
<v Examiner>The hormonal control of spermatogenesis, and testosterone.

2
00:00:05.624 --> 00:00:06.423
<v Examiner>Five marks.

3
00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:10.199
<v Examiner>Describe the hormonal control of spermatogenesis,

4
00:00:10.199 --> 00:00:14.340
<v Examiner>and the physiological effects of testosterone during puberty.

5
00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.760
The hook: GnRH, then FSH and LH.

6
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.823
L for Leydig, T for testosterone.

7
00:00:20.823 --> 00:00:23.515
S for Sertoli, I for inhibin.

8
00:00:23.965 --> 00:00:25.197
From the brain.

9
00:00:25.197 --> 00:00:30.369
The hypothalamus releases GnRH, gonadotropin-releasing hormone,

10
00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:34.803
which makes the anterior pituitary release FSH and LH.

11
00:00:35.253 --> 00:00:36.259
At the testes.

12
00:00:36.259 --> 00:00:42.368
LH stimulates the Leydig cells, also called interstitial cells, to make testosterone,

13
00:00:42.368 --> 00:00:45.674
a lipid-soluble hormone made from cholesterol.

14
00:00:45.674 --> 00:00:48.405
Testosterone enhances spermatogenesis.

15
00:00:48.405 --> 00:00:52.933
FSH acts on the Sertoli cells, also called sustentacular cells,

16
00:00:52.933 --> 00:00:57.461
which nourish the developing sperm and support spermatogenesis.

17
00:00:58.911 --> 00:01:00.233
Negative feedback.

18
00:01:00.233 --> 00:01:05.009
Testosterone switches off the hypothalamus, so there's less GnRH,

19
00:01:05.009 --> 00:01:08.462
and the anterior pituitary, so there's less LH.

20
00:01:08.462 --> 00:01:12.135
Inhibin, from the Sertoli cells, switches off FSH.

21
00:01:12.135 --> 00:01:14.633
That keeps the sperm count steady.

22
00:01:15.083 --> 00:01:16.685
Testosterone at puberty.

23
00:01:16.685 --> 00:01:19.821
It grows the reproductive organs to adult size,

24
00:01:19.821 --> 00:01:25.026
and brings the secondary sex characteristics: pubic, axillary and facial hair,

25
00:01:25.026 --> 00:01:28.829
a deeper voice, a bigger chest, and thicker, oilier skin.

26
00:01:28.829 --> 00:01:32.232
It increases bone density and skeletal muscle mass.

27
00:01:32.232 --> 00:01:35.969
And it's the basis of libido, in both males and females.

28
00:01:36.419 --> 00:01:37.344
And in females?

29
00:01:37.344 --> 00:01:41.480
Her student-marked quiz asks for testosterone in males and females,

30
00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.516
and her model answer covers both.

31
00:01:43.516 --> 00:01:48.515
Testosterone has lots of effects around the body, and we see them in females too,

32
00:01:48.515 --> 00:01:51.540
because the adrenal glands can make testosterone.

33
00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.662
In men, it's thought to regulate sex drive, or libido, bone mass, fat distribution,

34
00:01:56.662 --> 00:02:01.229
muscle mass and strength, and the production of red blood cells and sperm.

35
00:02:02.679 --> 00:02:03.486
The traps.

36
00:02:03.486 --> 00:02:07.119
Leydig cells make testosterone, driven by LH.

37
00:02:07.119 --> 00:02:12.285
Sertoli cells nourish the sperm and make inhibin, driven by FSH.

38
00:02:12.285 --> 00:02:13.576
Don't swap them.

39
00:02:13.576 --> 00:02:19.226
Second: inhibin controls FSH, while testosterone controls GnRH and LH.

40
00:02:19.226 --> 00:02:21.728
Third: give the chain in order.

41
00:02:21.728 --> 00:02:24.311
Hypothalamus, pituitary, testes.

42
00:02:24.761 --> 00:02:25.333
<v Examiner>Once more.

43
00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:26.361
<v Examiner>The male hormones.

44
00:02:28.811 --> 00:02:34.412
The hypothalamus releases GnRH, so the anterior pituitary releases FSH and LH.

45
00:02:34.412 --> 00:02:40.443
LH stimulates the Leydig cells to make testosterone, which enhances spermatogenesis.

46
00:02:40.443 --> 00:02:44.392
FSH acts on the Sertoli cells, which nourish the sperm.

47
00:02:44.392 --> 00:02:47.982
Testosterone feeds back to switch off GnRH and LH,

48
00:02:47.982 --> 00:02:51.715
and inhibin from the Sertoli cells switches off FSH.

49
00:02:51.715 --> 00:02:56.956
At puberty, testosterone grows the reproductive organs, and brings pubic,

50
00:02:56.956 --> 00:03:03.275
axillary and facial hair, a deeper voice, more bone density and muscle mass, and libido.

51
00:03:03.275 --> 00:03:09.665
Females make testosterone too, in the adrenal glands, and it drives libido in both sexes.
